  "query_preview": "..\n\nLarge scale pattern will remain governed by lower amplitude mid \nlevel west-northwest featuring copious minor perturbations through \nmid week period. Low level frontal boundary effectively stalled near \nthe IN/OH/MI state line marking the northern expanse of the deeper \ninstability reservoir that resides just to the south. Pockets of \nconvective development may continue to manifest this morning in the \nvicinity of the boundary, particularly as the low level jet folds \ninto the existing frontal slope. This will offer a lower probability \nfor mainly areas of south of I-94 to witness some early day \nactivity. Otherwise, attention today squarely on behavior of the \nconvective episode now organizing across South Dakota. Backed by a \npronounced vort max and extremely receptive downstream environment, \ngeneral expectation remains for a forward propagating MCS to \naccelerate into southern WI/northern IL by midday. From there, \nconfidence in trajectory declines as a subset of the model solution \nspace shows preference toward a path into the deeper instability \nparked to the south, while others do allow at least a portion of the \nsystem to arrive locally during the mid afternoon to early evening \nwindow. Greater potential with southward extent /particularly \nbetween the I-94 corridor and Ohio border/, where adequate deep \nlayer shear and MLcape in excess of 2000 j/kg would support deeper \nconvective organization with an associated damaging wind gust risk. \nConditional localized heavy rainfall threat also certainly exists. \nHigh temperatures low to mid 80s again today.  \n\nStagnant large scale pattern ensures similar underlying \nthermodynamic conditions exist both Wednesday and Thursday. \nConvective potential within this environment continues to carry \nstrong reliance on finding tangible forced ascent in the form of \nadditional shortwave energy to engage a profile featuring a standard \ndegree of diurnal destabilization for mid August. Perusal of model \nguidance establishes little confidence in offering a more targeted \nopportunity. Absent of this, expectation for generally dry \nconditions to hold outside of perhaps a smaller scale response along \nany lake breeze activity. Outgoing forecast offers a more broad \nbrushed chance mention highlighting the peak heating window each \nday.  \n\nHigh pressure briefly increases influence by Friday beneath \nconfluence mid level northwest flow. This offers dry conditions to \nfinish the week, as deep layer subsidence exists within a slight \ncooler and less humid conditions. Shortwave upper ridge will roll \ninto the region Friday night and linger into at least the first half \nof the weekend. There is potential for a ridge running wave to lift \nacross the region over the weekend, but again carries low \npredictable at this stage. Temperatures over the weekend generally \nremain seasonable.",
